pharmaceutical and biotechnology companies in particular, have historically experienced extreme price and volume
fluctuations. These fluctuations often have been unrelated or disproportionate to the operating performance of these
companies. These broad market and industry factors could reduce the market price of our Common Stock, regardless
of our actual operating performance.
